{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe typed reconciler payload work (earthborn-statuelike-boutu) introduces a named direction/action payload union and threads it through the planner, coordinator, and adapter-projection seam. The modules that build and project those payloads are already within a handful of lines of the hard 800-LOC module-size cap (`.github/module-size-limit.txt` = 800), so that expand would breach the CI module-size gate on first edit:\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/run_differs.py` = 798 (43 payload/mutation references)\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py` = 793\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py` = 793\n\nCreate headroom FIRST as a behavior-preserving extraction along existing call-graph seams, so the typed cutover lands without fighting the module-size gate. This story adds no typed-payload logic; it only relocates existing clusters.\n\n## Approach\n\nExtract cohesive, already-clustered helpers into sibling modules per the AGENTS.md module-size policy (existing call-graph seams only; target 200-500 LOC; never create a module < 100 LOC; never split mechanically to hit a number):\n\n- `run_differs.py`: move the self-contained outbound sub-pass (`_run_differs_outbound` plus its alert emitters `_emit_outbound_field_alerts` / `_emit_recovery_failure_alerts`) into a sibling module.\n- `outbound_differ.py`: move the memoized effective-mapping resolvers (`_memoize_effective`, `_effective_status_map_for`, `_effective_type_map_for`, `_effective_priority_map_for`, `_effective_create_defaults_for`, `_effective_link_map_for`, `_effective_excluded_sync_types_for`) into a sibling module.\n- `applier.py`: DEFAULT to extracting the cross-project/drift cluster (`HeadDriftError`, `CrossProjectTargetError`, `_cross_project_targets`, `_recheck_drift`) — it is fully self-contained (no back-edge into `applier.py` needed at all) and yields ~793→~723 LOC. Fall back to the batch-execution cluster (`_apply_batch`, `_apply_one`, `_print_batch_recon`) only if the drift cluster's headroom proves insufficient once the typed cutover lands; that cluster instead calls back into `applier.py`-resident symbols (`_cross_project_targets`, `HeadDriftError`, `_load_acli`, `_load_concurrency`, `BatchApplyContext`, etc.), so choosing it requires re-exporting those back-references too.\n\n**Re-export requirement (this is the load-bearing constraint the plan must commit to):** every symbol relocated out of `applier.py` or `run_differs.py` MUST be re-exported back into the ORIGINAL module via a top-level `from <sibling> import <name>  # noqa: F401` (mirroring the pattern already used repeatedly in both files — e.g. `outbound_differ.py`'s `outbound_assignee`/`outbound_comments`/`outbound_labels`/`outbound_links` splits, and `applier.py`'s own `apply_base`/`apply_handlers`/`apply_outbound`/`batch_dispatch`/`pass_io`/`rebar_id_audit`/`typed_dispatch` splits), AND the resident internal caller (`run_differs()`'s call to `_run_differs_outbound`; `_apply_batch`'s/`_apply_one`'s calls to `_recheck_drift`/`_cross_project_targets`) must keep resolving that symbol via the ORIGINAL module's own globals (a bare-name reference, not a qualified `sibling.name()` call), so it still binds to whatever is currently in that module's namespace at call time. This is required because:\n\n- Multiple unit tests patch/reference the to-be-moved symbols through the ORIGINAL module namespace by attribute name — invisible to LSP structural-reference tools, found only by a string-name grep sweep:\n  - `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_apply_batch_drift_tolerance.py:329` `pytest.raises(applier.HeadDriftError)`; `:247` `applier._apply_batch(...)`\n  - `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/conflict/test_conflict_filing_deferred.py:188` `monkeypatch.setattr(applier, \"_apply_batch\", ...)`\n  - `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_applier_cross_project_guard.py:129` `pytest.raises(applier_mod.CrossProjectTargetError)`\n  - `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_live_mode_failure_tally.py:677` `monkeypatch.setattr(applier, \"_recheck_drift\", hostile_drift)`\n  - `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_snapshot_differ_stale_local_state.py:113`, `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_run_differs_wires_refresh_scoped_snapshot_79a4.py:89`, `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_ticket_plan_shadow.py:426` — all `monkeypatch.setattr(run_differs_mod, \"_run_differs_outbound\", ...)`\n- A production in-package consumer also reads the relocated symbol off the ORIGINAL module by attribute, not by direct import: `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/batch_dispatch.py:425` `return (applier.HeadDriftError, pass_io.RescheduleError, urllib.error.HTTPError)`, where `applier` is itself `lazy_load(\"rebar_reconciler.applier\", \"applier.py\")` at `batch_dispatch.py:423`. `HeadDriftError` MUST remain resolvable as `applier.HeadDriftError` after relocation.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_mutation_builders.py:20-28` imports the five `_effective_*_for` resolvers from `outbound_differ` (`from rebar_reconciler.outbound_differ import (...)`) — this production caller's import path is unaffected by the re-export (it keeps importing from `outbound_differ`, which re-exports from the new sibling), but is named here for completeness of the reference inventory.\n\nPublic entry points and import paths keep working via this re-export; only internal call sites' IMPLEMENTATION moves — the call sites' NAMESPACE resolution (`applier.<name>`, `run_differs.<name>`) does not.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` — extract the named clusters into new sibling modules; re-export each relocated symbol back into its original module (top-level import), and update imports only elsewhere.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` — import-path updates only; no assertion changes. Tests that patch/read the ORIGINAL module namespace (enumerated above) require NO changes at all, because the re-export requirement above keeps `applier.<name>` / `run_differs.<name>` resolving.\n\n## Testing\n\nExisting reconciler unit/integration suites pass unchanged (behavior-preserving), including every string-keyed `monkeypatch.setattr`/`patch.object`/`pytest.raises` call site enumerated above. Module-size gate and per-function complexity ratchet pass. Lint and typecheck pass. No new CI-provider, network, Docker, or Jira dependency is introduced (portable default suite).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `run_differs.py`, `outbound_differ.py`, and `applier.py` are each comfortably below 800 LOC (target <= 700) with room for the typed union, achieved only by extracting existing call-graph clusters into sibling modules.\n- [ ] No newly created module is below 100 LOC, and no extraction is mechanical: each sibling is a cluster whose members already called one another.\n- [ ] Every relocated symbol is re-exported back into its original module (`applier.py` / `outbound_differ.py` / `run_differs.py`) via a top-level import, and every internal caller in that original module resolves the symbol via a bare/module-namespace reference (not a qualified sibling-module call), so `applier.HeadDriftError`, `applier.CrossProjectTargetError`, `applier._apply_batch` (if that cluster is chosen), `applier._cross_project_targets`, `applier._recheck_drift`, `run_differs._run_differs_outbound`, `run_differs._emit_outbound_field_alerts`, `run_differs._emit_recovery_failure_alerts`, and `outbound_differ._effective_status_map_for` (+ its five siblings) + `outbound_differ._memoize_effective` all keep resolving, and every enumerated monkeypatch/patch.object/pytest.raises site above continues to intercept/raise correctly with zero test-assertion changes.\n- [ ] `batch_dispatch.py`'s `applier.HeadDriftError` attribute read (via its own `lazy_load(\"rebar_reconciler.applier\", ...)`) keeps resolving after the applier.py extraction.\n- [ ] Behavior is unchanged: existing reconciler test suites pass with no edits beyond import paths.\n- [ ] Module-size gate, per-function complexity ratchet, lint, and typecheck all pass.\n- [ ] No production write-route change and no typed-payload/union logic is introduced here; that remains earthborn-statuelike-boutu."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788063747278724001,"uuid":"cdfc0520-1aaa-49fe-87ce-f2039dfde3f4"}